You are working on a branch which is adding virtual keyspaces to Vitess.

Previously vitess could only handle one keyspace/shard per tablet, but in this branch there can be multiple.

For the implementation, existing keyspaces are said to be "physical keyspaces", and a "virtual keyspace" can be added to any physical. Each virtual keyspace is a new schema that is created on the tablet.

Virtual keyspaces do not have shards - the code needs to first lookup the physical keyspace and then find the tablet from there (primary, replica etc).

This affects a lot of components because the vttablet has a lot of strong dependencies/expectations on there only being one dbName with data. We need to fix and remove all of those.

If you want to run the tests, you first need to run make in this root directory and set the environment variable VTROOT. i.e.

```
export VTROOT=~/go/src/github.com/morgo/vitess/
cd $VTROOT
make
```


Because the tests take a long time to run, after you've done this it's better of testing package-by-package, and set a timeout for each test of 1 minute.